messages:
Maria L: Pushed a quick figma update for the dark console — trying a 'slate' palette with softer syntax highlights and three chart color ramps. Link: https://www.figma.com/file/xxxx/dark-console-slate
Sam K: looked — nice direction. can we raise the foreground contrast for inline code? the current blue on #0f1316 is a bit low.
June Park: Agree with Sam. Also the legend markers are almost invisible at small sizes. Might need bolder strokes or a higher-luminance fill.
Ellie (token-team): Quick accessibility check — heading text contrast against bg #0b0f11 is 4.2:1 right now. We want 4.5:1 minimum. If we bump headings white to #e7eef0 that gets us to ~4.6.
Patrick D: For charts, I prefer using a desaturated orange for primary instead of bright coral — less alarming on dashboards. Proposal: primary #ff9f66 -> try #e68a4a. Secondary stays teal #4bd1c6?
Maria L: Thanks. Updated tokens in figma: --bg-900: #0b0f11; --fg-100: #e7eef0; --code-bg: #0f1316; --code-fg: #7fd1ff; --chart-primary: #e68a4a; --chart-secondary: #4bd1c6;
Sam K: Can you paste the CSS vars here so I can try locally?
Maria L: sure — paste below
```css
:root {
  --bg-900: #0b0f11;
  --bg-800: #0f1316;
  --fg-100: #e7eef0;
  --muted-60: #8b98a1;
  --code-bg: #0f1316;
  --code-fg: #7fd1ff;
  --syntax-keyword: #b59fff;
  --syntax-string: #a6e6a1;
  --chart-primary: #e68a4a;
  --chart-secondary: #4bd1c6;
  --chart-ternary: #9aa6ff;
}
```
June Park: Nice. Quick visual nit — the string color feels very bright compared to the muted text, maybe pull string from #a6e6a1 -> #8fd08a? Keeps distinction but less neon.
Ellie (token-team): Ran a contrast sim: code inline bg+fg pair (#0f1316 / #7fd1ff) meets AA for large text but fails for 12px small labels. Suggest increasing code-fg to #9fe8ff or adding subtle outline.
Patrick D: For the legend markers: try 2px stroke of alpha black at 8% over each marker — makes them pop on patterned backgrounds.
Maria L: Updated again in figma and pushed a small screenshot. Also added a variant for high-contrast mode (HC tokens).
theme-bot: Accessibility scan complete — found 3 issues: heading contrast, inline-code small text, chart color proximity. See /a11y/report/1798123456
Sam K: great. I'll QA the high-contrast variant in next dev pass. If results are good we can ship as opt-in toggle in feature flags. :thumbsup:
June Park: One more request — can we test chart colors with daltonism simulator? Some of our customers use red-green palates.
Maria L: added daltonism frames in figma. please check the frames named 'protanopia' and 'deuteranopia'
Ellie (token-team): LGTM with the tweaks. I'll update the token docs and add a note about small-label code usage patterns.
Patrick D: thumbs up. If no objections, I'll land the chart palette change in the next release branch.
Maria L: thanks everyone — iterate tomorrow after QA feedback. :coffee:
